  "rationale": "With no mitigations, RCE is reachable along one linear chain: inject_jndi_string, trigger_jndi_lookup, resolve_to_attacker, return_malicious_reference, load_class_via_gadget, execute_payload. load_class_via_reference is already blocked because trust_url_codebase=false, so trust_url_codebase_false adds nothing; the gadget path still works. Zero mitigations is therefore not enough. Every step before the final branch is a single point of failure, so one mitigation suffices. For example, formatMsgNoLookups (message_lookups=false) blocks trigger_jndi_lookup, which cuts every downstream step. disable_jndi, remove_jndi_class, block_egress or input_validation would each work alone in the same way. The minimum is 1. This assumes each mitigation name maps to the configuration constant it obviously disables; the model does not state these mappings explicitly."
